{
  "description": "Applying one overlay. 'facts' describe the consumer: os, root, identity, state (its state directory), pinned, grants (what this overlay may read, by provider: secret names, file keys, host variables), base_env (the environment being built), host_env (its own), secrets (named), secret_files (the secrets directory), files (env file contents), providers, env_scripts_enabled, enforces_network. 'expect' gives the resulting environment, the selected setup and runtime variants, what a probe needs, and the weakenings as [id, subject]; or the refusal.",
  "spec": "spec/v0/environment.md#order-of-application",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "bare",
      "description": "No manifest: only the root variable; unpinned is reported.",
      "manifest": {},
